Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 16:37:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] port: fix DSPARK routing-replay capture (slice pitch +
 result passthrough)

Two independent defects zeroed every response token's captured routing
under DSPARK (trainer replay then consumed expert-0 rows: train logprob
-3.8/-6.5 vs rollout -0.24; capture-content probes showed 98-99% zero rows).

1) dp-attention capture slice pitch under spec-verify graphs:
   get_dp_local_slice_cpu uses cuda_graph_batch as the per-rank row pitch
   of the gathered capture buffer. model_runner passed runner.bs (REQUEST
   batch), but target-verify graphs lay out bs * num_tokens_per_bs
   token-rows per rank (num_tokens_per_bs = draft width W). Every dp rank
   except 0 sliced unwritten buffer (upstream's own 'FIXME: spec decoding
   num_verify_tokens not accounted for'). Pass bs * num_tokens_per_bs
   (x1 for plain decode, unchanged).

2) DSpark/DFlash verify-result rebuild dropped capture outputs:
   _forward_decode constructs a fresh GenerationBatchResult after verify;
   the inner target forward's deferred routed_experts_output /
   indexer_topk_output were never carried over, so the accepted-row filter
   never ran and host-cache verify rows stayed zero. Thread both fields
   through TargetVerifyResult (both executor return sites) and both
   workers' GenerationBatchResult.

Fixed-data evidence: 32/32 samples healthy (response rows 7.6% zeros ==
prompt-row natural rate); filter sees stride=6 slices at 93% nonzero.
